# GOLDEN RCleaned ROverlapReq POSSIBLY
# GROUND-TRUTH: the cleaning idiom. reject dR<0.4 fires exactly when select dR<0.4 passes
#   (min pairwise dR), so the two regions are complementary on that predicate -> TRULY
#   DISJOINT, even over events with absent eta/phi (a soft-false dR<0.4 excludes
#   ROverlapReq and admits RCleaned - complements of ONE predicate cannot both hold).
#   In ROverlapReq: {jet eta0 phi0, ele eta0 phi0.1}=dR0.1. In RCleaned: same jet, ele eta2 (dR2).
#
#   The pin is the fail-closed POSSIBLY: the absent-property guard (2026-07-25)
#   degrades any negation over a possibly-absent quantity to Unknown, because in
#   general `reject q < k` HOLDS on absence while its classical encoding excludes
#   it (two complementary rejects fabricated a PROVEN DISJOINT). The guard cannot
#   see that THIS pair negates the same predicate it selects. Definedness
#   (presence) modeling - SOUNDNESS_PROOF_2026-07-25 s8 item 1 - re-proves this
#   pair exactly; flip the pin back to DISJOINT when it lands.

object jets
  take Jet
  select pt > 30

object eles
  take Ele
  select pt > 20

region RCleaned
  select size(jets) >= 1
  select size(eles) >= 1
  reject dR(jets, eles) < 0.4

region ROverlapReq
  select size(jets) >= 1
  select size(eles) >= 1
  select dR(jets, eles) < 0.4
